          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Propositions and their Converses"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.716,
            0.068,
            0.866,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": []
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.757,
            0.174,
            0.823,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "0905CH09"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.259,
            0.484,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the following statement:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.284,
            0.881,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Statement 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If two sides of a triangle are equal, then the angles opposite the equal sides are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.328,
            0.872,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Such a statement that is either true or false is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "proposition",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Now consider the following proposition:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.372,
            0.881,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Statement 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If two angles of a triangle are equal, then the sides opposite the equal angles have equal lengths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.416,
            0.882,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first proposition is of the form ‘if X then Y’. The second is of the form ‘if Y then X’. We say that the second proposition is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "converse",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the first proposition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.474,
            0.881,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The statement ‘if X then Y’ is also written as ‘X "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "implies",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Y’. We will use both formulations interchangeably."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.512,
            0.756,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If a proposition is true, then is its converse always true?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.549,
            0.401,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.585,
            0.851,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have proved the first statement in an earlier grade. Is the second statement true? Can you prove it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.628,
            0.802,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Draw the altitude from the vertex containing the third angle.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.665,
            0.842,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider some examples of propositions and their converses,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.69,
            0.287,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.708,
            0.679,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Proposition P: If it rains, then the road is wet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.728,
            0.715,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Converse Q: If the road is wet, then it has rained."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.753,
            0.881,
            0.792
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proposition P is true but its converse, Q, may not be true. For instance, the road may be wet because a tanker spilled water on the road!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.797,
            0.882,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A situation that illustrates why a given proposition is not necessarily true is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "counterexample",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". It refers to an example that contradicts the stated proposition."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
